1
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,440
I'll be waiting for good news!

2
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:09,160
Make sure you bring back that million.

3
00:00:11,560 --> 00:00:12,840
Good night.

4
00:00:15,440 --> 00:00:19,360
<i>Everyone must live</i>
<i>and play the game here for seven days.</i>

5
00:00:19,440 --> 00:00:21,240
<i>Whoever is the last one standing</i>

6
00:00:21,320 --> 00:00:23,560
<i>will take home a prize of</i>
<i>ten million baht.</i>

7
00:00:23,640 --> 00:00:24,600
Hey.

8
00:00:24,680 --> 00:00:25,800
<i>It's because of him, isn't it?</i>

9
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:27,280
<i>The one named Pee.</i>

10
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:29,400
I can't live without him.

11
00:00:29,480 --> 00:00:31,600
<i>But you still have me.</i>

12
00:00:31,680 --> 00:00:33,880
<i>I told you not to trust</i>
<i>anyone in this game.</i>

13
00:01:01,280 --> 00:01:02,520
Fuck!

14
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:05,800
They got rid of the bodies so fast.

15
00:01:05,880 --> 00:01:08,600
It's like a game. When someone dies,
they just disappear.

16
00:01:08,680 --> 00:01:10,560
Are you still going to defend them

17
00:01:10,640 --> 00:01:12,520
and say it's just a reality show?

18
00:01:15,360 --> 00:01:17,120
Are we gonna make it out of here alive?

19
00:01:23,080 --> 00:01:25,680
Don't forget, I'm the bodyguard.

20
00:01:25,760 --> 00:01:28,720
Of course I can keep you safe.

21
00:01:31,520 --> 00:01:34,520
But you're not mad I chose to
save Wut last round, right?

22
00:01:36,520 --> 00:01:37,640
I understand.

23
00:01:38,600 --> 00:01:40,080
If you keep choosing me,

24
00:01:40,880 --> 00:01:43,120
everyone will figure out
you're the bodyguard.

25
00:01:46,920 --> 00:01:48,080
You've got a point.

26
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:53,120
We're practically inseparable.

27
00:01:53,200 --> 00:01:54,720
It wouldn't be hard to guess.

28
00:02:00,080 --> 00:02:01,720
But you need to look after yourself too.

29
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:03,600
Don't just worry about me.

30
00:02:03,680 --> 00:02:05,920
What? Who's worried about you?

31
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:08,479
I'm the bodyguard.

32
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:10,600
As long as I protect myself every round,

33
00:02:10,680 --> 00:02:12,000
I'll survive.

34
00:02:13,080 --> 00:02:15,080
Yeah, whatever.

35
00:02:16,640 --> 00:02:18,520
And if those damn wolves come after me,

36
00:02:19,080 --> 00:02:20,800
I'll fight back for sure.

37
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:25,560
But I'd rather escape from here.

38
00:02:25,640 --> 00:02:26,920
Let's not risk it.

39
00:02:27,600 --> 00:02:28,880
How are you gonna escape?

40
00:02:28,960 --> 00:02:31,360
Those damn rabbits are all over the house.

41
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:33,720
I've seen them. They're all good shots.

42
00:02:37,200 --> 00:02:39,520
But I think they must have some weakness.

43
00:02:41,200 --> 00:02:43,960
For now, you and I have to play along.

44
00:02:44,040 --> 00:02:45,600
Don't let them catch on.

45
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:52,520
Ten million isn't fucking worth it.

46
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:01,200
Oh, right. While you were hiding,

47
00:03:01,280 --> 00:03:02,920
did you see the wolf's face?

48
00:03:03,480 --> 00:03:04,800
I didn't see his face.

49
00:03:05,880 --> 00:03:07,280
I only saw his legs.

50
00:03:11,480 --> 00:03:13,800
But I'm sure he's a man.

51
00:03:21,880 --> 00:03:23,400
We'd better hide inside for now.

52
00:03:32,200 --> 00:03:33,040
Come on.

53
00:06:00,720 --> 00:06:02,240
You're up early.

54
00:06:02,320 --> 00:06:04,120
I thought you said you were a night owl.

55
00:06:06,160 --> 00:06:07,360
What about you?

56
00:06:07,440 --> 00:06:10,720
Don't writers usually wake up
in the afternoon?

57
00:06:12,000 --> 00:06:13,240
I'm the exception.

58
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:18,520
Do you wake up this early every day?

59
00:06:20,320 --> 00:06:23,040
Not really. I can't sleep.

60
00:06:25,720 --> 00:06:26,920
How many days?

61
00:06:30,120 --> 00:06:32,920
I mean, how many days
have you been unable to sleep?

62
00:06:36,120 --> 00:06:37,640
I don't know.

63
00:06:37,720 --> 00:06:38,920
I haven't been counting.

64
00:06:39,920 --> 00:06:42,840
I take medication,
but it doesn't seem to work.

65
00:06:43,960 --> 00:06:46,240
I have to wait until sunrise

66
00:06:47,800 --> 00:06:50,720
before I can feel at ease
and get some sleep.

67
00:06:54,040 --> 00:06:57,040
Or maybe… you're a vampire.

68
00:06:58,320 --> 00:07:00,240
Awake at night, asleep during the day.

69
00:07:00,320 --> 00:07:01,640
Allergic to sunlight and all that.

70
00:07:01,720 --> 00:07:03,120
Let me see your fangs.

71
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:06,440
You've got a wilder imagination
than a novelist like me.

72
00:07:07,120 --> 00:07:08,560
Well, I spend so much time with you.

73
00:07:08,640 --> 00:07:09,920
I have to adapt a little.

74
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:19,720
Whenever you're ready,

75
00:07:19,800 --> 00:07:21,200
you can tell me about it.

76
00:08:27,160 --> 00:08:28,720
LAY LAMOE BEACH BAR

77
00:08:28,800 --> 00:08:30,160
I'm hungry.

78
00:08:30,920 --> 00:08:31,920
What should we eat?

79
00:08:32,600 --> 00:08:34,799
- Let's see what they have inside.
- Okay.

80
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:42,640
Perfect timing, Talay, Sun.

81
00:08:42,720 --> 00:08:45,680
I have to go to Bangkok
for a couple of days.

82
00:08:45,760 --> 00:08:49,720
If… you want anything to eat
or drink, it's all in the fridge.

83
00:08:49,800 --> 00:08:52,520
- Take care of the place. Bye!
- Sure.

84
00:08:53,600 --> 00:08:56,320
- Shall we check the kitchen?
- Sure, let's go.

85
00:09:39,080 --> 00:09:40,800
Between the rice porridge and me,

86
00:09:41,640 --> 00:09:42,800
which tastes better?

87
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:47,720
The rice porridge, obviously.

88
00:09:47,800 --> 00:09:49,000
This early in the morning,

89
00:09:49,080 --> 00:09:51,920
something hot goes down
smoothly and refreshes me.

90
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:53,840
But someone like you,

91
00:09:53,920 --> 00:09:56,240
I'd need lots of water to wash you down.

92
00:09:56,320 --> 00:09:57,640
You're too dry.

93
00:10:00,920 --> 00:10:02,640
You weren't like this last night.

94
00:10:03,520 --> 00:10:05,600
I thought I was pretty hot.

95
00:10:12,200 --> 00:10:13,720
But that person's name is Pee, right?

96
00:10:17,120 --> 00:10:19,040
You even searched for news about him?

97
00:10:21,440 --> 00:10:22,520
Is he your ex?

98
00:10:26,120 --> 00:10:27,520
He used to be my assistant.

99
00:10:31,400 --> 00:10:33,120
Judging by your reaction,

100
00:10:34,400 --> 00:10:36,240
he wasn't just an assistant.

101
00:10:41,440 --> 00:10:44,120
To me, that's true.

102
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:45,640
He was more than an assistant.

103
00:10:46,600 --> 00:10:50,160
But to him, I never meant anything.

104
00:10:51,320 --> 00:10:53,040
You got your heart broken,

105
00:10:53,120 --> 00:10:55,000
so you can't write romance novels anymore?

106
00:10:56,520 --> 00:10:58,080
That's not like you at all.

107
00:10:58,160 --> 00:11:00,320
Just because one person let you down

108
00:11:00,400 --> 00:11:03,160
doesn't mean your
whole world has to fall apart.

109
00:11:06,120 --> 00:11:07,320
What about you?

110
00:11:07,400 --> 00:11:09,960
You keep playing hard to get,
refusing my offer.

111
00:11:10,040 --> 00:11:12,360
And I can see you drawing boundaries.

112
00:11:12,440 --> 00:11:14,120
You've built walls.

113
00:11:14,200 --> 00:11:16,560
You refuse to date anyone.

114
00:11:17,200 --> 00:11:20,200
Are you saying you've never been hurt?

115
00:11:20,280 --> 00:11:23,320
Why? Come on, tell me.

116
00:11:23,400 --> 00:11:25,440
Who broke your heart so badly

117
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:28,160
that you don't believe in love anymore?

118
00:11:29,400 --> 00:11:30,760
You don't need to know.

119
00:11:32,320 --> 00:11:34,440
But things are good between us like this.

120
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:37,520
No labels. No commitments.

121
00:11:38,720 --> 00:11:41,000
And we can't hurt each other

122
00:11:41,920 --> 00:11:43,400
because we're nothing to each other.

123
00:11:44,040 --> 00:11:46,760
What do you think?
Sounds fair, doesn't it?

124
00:11:48,800 --> 00:11:51,640
So… we only share the good times,

125
00:11:51,720 --> 00:11:52,920
not the bad? Is that it?

126
00:12:04,800 --> 00:12:07,560
And when you told me last night

127
00:12:07,640 --> 00:12:08,920
that I still had you…

128
00:12:11,720 --> 00:12:14,600
was that part of pretending
we were dating too?

129
00:12:19,600 --> 00:12:20,600
Yes.

130
00:12:21,320 --> 00:12:22,400
I guess it was.

131
00:12:51,800 --> 00:12:53,600
<i>The first night is over.</i>

132
00:12:54,240 --> 00:12:57,320
<i>All remaining players,</i>
<i>please proceed to the dining room.</i>

133
00:13:03,600 --> 00:13:04,640
Yoyeh.

134
00:13:05,440 --> 00:13:06,440
Yoyeh.

135
00:13:07,200 --> 00:13:08,200
Wake up.

136
00:13:16,800 --> 00:13:17,800
Is it over?

137
00:13:56,040 --> 00:13:57,440
- I'm starving.
- Me too.

138
00:13:57,520 --> 00:13:59,040
- Seriously.
- What is there to eat?

139
00:13:59,120 --> 00:14:00,120
Here.

140
00:14:14,560 --> 00:14:15,800
Here it is.

141
00:14:33,720 --> 00:14:35,440
How can anyone eat after seeing that?

142
00:14:45,320 --> 00:14:47,840
Hey. Don't worry.

143
00:14:47,920 --> 00:14:49,680
Neither of us is a wolf.

144
00:14:50,320 --> 00:14:52,400
We almost got killed yesterday.

145
00:14:53,400 --> 00:14:54,720
Luckily, we survived.

146
00:14:55,800 --> 00:14:56,800
Really?

147
00:14:57,400 --> 00:15:00,520
Then… why are you two always together?

148
00:15:01,520 --> 00:15:02,720
Are you two dating?

149
00:15:03,400 --> 00:15:04,520
- No.
- No.

150
00:15:08,240 --> 00:15:09,720
We're just old friends.

151
00:15:11,200 --> 00:15:12,720
You're friends.

152
00:15:12,800 --> 00:15:17,000
But… you and that guy named Cha
are friends too, right?

153
00:15:19,440 --> 00:15:21,280
That asshole?
Don't count him as my friend.

154
00:15:32,120 --> 00:15:35,120
I think… we should team up.

155
00:15:36,080 --> 00:15:37,440
Because at least,

156
00:15:37,520 --> 00:15:40,600
if tonight we vote out one wolf,

157
00:15:41,640 --> 00:15:43,520
there'll only be one wolf left.

158
00:15:44,440 --> 00:15:47,520
That means we can survive another night.

159
00:15:48,120 --> 00:15:49,240
Right.

160
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:52,760
One wolf left against six villagers.

161
00:15:52,840 --> 00:15:54,240
We can easily take him down together.

162
00:15:57,440 --> 00:15:59,240
You two saw the wolf last night?

163
00:15:59,320 --> 00:16:00,600
Tell me about it.

164
00:16:04,840 --> 00:16:06,640
I didn't actually see his face.

165
00:16:07,320 --> 00:16:08,840
We were hiding.

166
00:16:08,920 --> 00:16:11,440
But I'm sure he's a man.

167
00:16:12,240 --> 00:16:13,320
I agree.

168
00:16:13,840 --> 00:16:15,640
Last night,

169
00:16:15,720 --> 00:16:17,920
I saw the wolf's shadow
while he was hunting.

170
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:19,360
He was really tall.

171
00:16:19,440 --> 00:16:22,480
About 180 centimeters.

172
00:16:22,560 --> 00:16:25,120
I also think he's definitely a man.

173
00:16:26,800 --> 00:16:28,480
Then that leaves

174
00:16:28,560 --> 00:16:29,840
Au,

175
00:16:31,280 --> 00:16:32,440
Nack,

176
00:16:33,520 --> 00:16:34,640
and Cha.

177
00:16:38,400 --> 00:16:40,520
You can't say there
are only three suspects.

178
00:16:41,440 --> 00:16:42,800
There have to be five.

179
00:16:44,440 --> 00:16:46,560
Au, Nack,

180
00:16:46,640 --> 00:16:49,760
Cha, and you two.

181
00:16:49,840 --> 00:16:51,040
Hey!

182
00:16:51,120 --> 00:16:53,320
Actually, Wut too. That makes six.

183
00:16:54,320 --> 00:16:55,440
I'm not a wolf.

184
00:16:57,320 --> 00:16:58,640
Who knows?

185
00:16:58,720 --> 00:17:02,720
Maybe you two are lying.

186
00:17:04,200 --> 00:17:06,359
I'm not going to throw my life away here.

187
00:17:15,119 --> 00:17:16,920
Good morning. It's day two.

188
00:17:18,240 --> 00:17:21,720
There are now eight players remaining.

189
00:17:22,760 --> 00:17:25,359
Please enjoy the food

190
00:17:25,440 --> 00:17:27,119
and comfortable beds we've provided.

191
00:17:27,800 --> 00:17:29,160
I ate better than this at the club.

192
00:17:30,320 --> 00:17:31,720
At 3 p.m. today,

193
00:17:31,800 --> 00:17:33,600
we'll play Capture the Flag.

194
00:17:34,360 --> 00:17:35,520
Capture the Flag?

195
00:17:36,520 --> 00:17:38,440
- What's that?
- We'll divide you into two teams,

196
00:17:38,520 --> 00:17:39,560
four players each.

197
00:17:39,640 --> 00:17:43,600
Each team must protect its own flag.

198
00:17:43,680 --> 00:17:45,920
One player will carry the flag,

199
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:47,680
while the other three
will devise a strategy

200
00:17:47,760 --> 00:17:50,040
to capture the opposing team's flag.

201
00:17:51,120 --> 00:17:52,560
The rule is,

202
00:17:52,640 --> 00:17:55,640
the opposing team cannot attack you

203
00:17:55,720 --> 00:17:57,440
unless you enter their territory.

204
00:17:58,200 --> 00:18:01,160
Most importantly, each player

205
00:18:01,240 --> 00:18:04,120
will wear a team-colored armband.

206
00:18:04,200 --> 00:18:05,960
If any player

207
00:18:06,040 --> 00:18:07,920
loses their armband to the opposing team,

208
00:18:08,520 --> 00:18:09,920
they're out.

209
00:18:10,640 --> 00:18:12,840
The staff have also drawn lots

210
00:18:12,920 --> 00:18:14,320
to assign you to teams.

211
00:18:14,760 --> 00:18:16,800
Team A will be on the left.

212
00:18:16,880 --> 00:18:19,560
The members are Natty,

213
00:18:20,200 --> 00:18:21,440
Tangmo,

214
00:18:22,520 --> 00:18:25,160
Wut, and Cha.

215
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:37,680
Team B will be on the right.

216
00:18:39,080 --> 00:18:41,640
The members are May,

217
00:18:44,320 --> 00:18:45,520
Nack,

218
00:18:47,640 --> 00:18:50,640
Au, and Yoyeh.

219
00:18:57,840 --> 00:18:59,800
Hey, what kind of team selection is this?

220
00:18:59,880 --> 00:19:02,360
You're putting me on the same team as Cha?

221
00:19:02,440 --> 00:19:04,480
- Because you're a pro.
- Pro, my ass!

222
00:19:04,560 --> 00:19:05,920
Can you two stop fighting already?

223
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:08,600
The staff's decision is final.

224
00:19:10,320 --> 00:19:11,760
Good luck, everyone.

225
00:19:14,720 --> 00:19:16,320
See you at 3 p.m.

226
00:19:17,440 --> 00:19:18,840
You damn butler!

227
00:19:18,920 --> 00:19:21,680
Hey, butler! I'm not staying on this team!

228
00:19:22,360 --> 00:19:25,240
- Hey, hey!
- Calm down, Tangmo. Just calm down.

229
00:19:25,920 --> 00:19:27,160
Listen to me first.

230
00:19:27,760 --> 00:19:29,200
This is actually better.

231
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:32,080
We can split up and find out who's a wolf.

232
00:20:23,440 --> 00:20:24,840
<i>The rule is,</i>

233
00:20:24,920 --> 00:20:28,560
<i>each team must protect its own flag.</i>

234
00:20:28,640 --> 00:20:29,640
<i>Most importantly,</i>

235
00:20:29,720 --> 00:20:33,280
<i>if any player</i>
<i>loses their armband to the opposing team,</i>

236
00:20:33,360 --> 00:20:35,440
<i>they're out.</i>

237
00:20:35,520 --> 00:20:36,640
<i>Good luck, everyone.</i>

238
00:20:37,840 --> 00:20:38,920
You.

239
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:40,320
Stay here and guard the flag with May.

240
00:20:40,400 --> 00:20:42,200
You'll only slow me down if you come.

241
00:20:42,800 --> 00:20:44,120
Let's all go together.

242
00:20:44,200 --> 00:20:47,200
They won't expect us to leave
the flag unguarded.

243
00:20:48,520 --> 00:20:49,720
Then why don't we split up?

244
00:20:49,800 --> 00:20:51,520
We can take them down together.

245
00:20:52,800 --> 00:20:55,320
No. Someone has to guard the flag.

246
00:21:02,920 --> 00:21:04,120
You stay here.

247
00:21:04,200 --> 00:21:06,320
Wut, come with me.

248
00:21:06,400 --> 00:21:08,600
- Okay.
- I want to come too.

249
00:21:09,520 --> 00:21:12,040
I may be small, but I'm good at dodging.

250
00:21:13,000 --> 00:21:14,480
You two can be the decoys,

251
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:16,200
and I'll grab the flag.

252
00:21:17,400 --> 00:21:19,440
Nobody needs to guard the flag.

253
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:21,680
Let's all go together.

254
00:21:22,320 --> 00:21:24,040
I agree.

255
00:21:24,120 --> 00:21:26,560
I think… they'll be surprised.

256
00:21:27,600 --> 00:21:29,240
Forget surprising them.

257
00:21:29,320 --> 00:21:30,760
They're already gone.

258
00:21:35,920 --> 00:21:37,400
Could they be using the same plan?

259
00:21:43,800 --> 00:21:45,160
If you want to win this game,

260
00:21:45,680 --> 00:21:47,400
we all have to work together.

261
00:21:52,840 --> 00:21:54,720
Let's go.

262
00:22:06,680 --> 00:22:07,920
Everyone, split up.

263
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:09,080
I'll check downstairs.

264
00:22:23,920 --> 00:22:25,480
What kind of plan is this?

265
00:22:28,200 --> 00:22:29,960
A plan to mess up your face.

266
00:22:52,840 --> 00:22:54,200
Let me go!

267
00:23:11,440 --> 00:23:12,960
Go cut them off over there.

268
00:23:16,320 --> 00:23:18,840
Player Au, out.

269
00:23:44,040 --> 00:23:45,640
Hey, stop!

270
00:23:45,720 --> 00:23:47,720
This is too easy.

271
00:23:47,800 --> 00:23:50,160
- Hey, you!
- And you came alone.

272
00:23:50,240 --> 00:23:51,360
Where are you going?

273
00:23:51,440 --> 00:23:52,760
Calm down, okay?

274
00:23:52,840 --> 00:23:53,920
Please let me go.

275
00:23:55,400 --> 00:23:56,400
Don't come any closer.

276
00:24:00,360 --> 00:24:01,760
What the fuck?!

277
00:24:01,840 --> 00:24:02,880
Fuck! Let me go!

278
00:24:03,960 --> 00:24:04,960
Oh, come on!

279
00:24:05,040 --> 00:24:07,320
- Aw, how pathetic.
- Hey, let me go!

280
00:24:07,400 --> 00:24:09,440
- Hey, hey!
- What was that?

281
00:24:09,520 --> 00:24:11,400
- Too easy, huh?
- You asshole!

282
00:24:13,520 --> 00:24:15,080
Piece of cake!

283
00:24:15,600 --> 00:24:17,080
Fuck you! I'll get you back!

284
00:24:17,720 --> 00:24:20,120
- Great plan!
<i>- Player Wut, out.</i>

285
00:25:10,520 --> 00:25:11,960
What the fuck are you doing?

286
00:25:12,040 --> 00:25:13,080
I told you.

287
00:25:13,160 --> 00:25:14,840
I'll win my own way.

288
00:25:14,920 --> 00:25:16,360
Motherfucker!

289
00:25:47,120 --> 00:25:48,120
Tangmo.

290
00:25:50,000 --> 00:25:51,160
Come play with me first.

291
00:26:00,120 --> 00:26:01,920
I give up! I give up!

292
00:26:16,720 --> 00:26:18,680
<i>Player Nack, out.</i>

293
00:27:11,720 --> 00:27:13,160
<i>Capture the Flag is over.</i>

294
00:27:14,040 --> 00:27:15,640
<i>The red team wins.</i>

295
00:28:11,320 --> 00:28:13,120
Congratulations, everyone.

296
00:28:14,520 --> 00:28:18,080
Now you must choose between
100,000 each in prize money

297
00:28:19,120 --> 00:28:21,080
or a clue as to who the wolves are.

298
00:28:21,160 --> 00:28:22,800
I'll take the clue.

299
00:28:23,960 --> 00:28:25,120
Let's take the money first.

300
00:28:26,120 --> 00:28:27,320
Who knows if the clue
will actually help us?

301
00:28:29,160 --> 00:28:31,040
I'd take the money too.

302
00:28:31,120 --> 00:28:32,960
That much money could keep me going.

303
00:28:33,040 --> 00:28:34,400
Why?

304
00:28:35,000 --> 00:28:36,680
Afraid they'll find out you're a wolf?

305
00:28:37,920 --> 00:28:38,920
That has nothing to do with it.

306
00:28:50,200 --> 00:28:52,560
I think… you should choose.

307
00:28:55,960 --> 00:28:57,440
I'll take the clue.

308
00:28:59,760 --> 00:29:00,840
Okay.

309
00:29:02,520 --> 00:29:03,520
Scholarship student.

310
00:29:08,600 --> 00:29:09,600
Scholarship student?

311
00:29:13,960 --> 00:29:15,120
How the fuck would anyone know?

312
00:29:36,320 --> 00:29:37,520
You fucker!

313
00:29:37,600 --> 00:29:41,280
I know you colluded with Tangmo.

314
00:29:41,360 --> 00:29:43,080
What the fuck are you talking about?

315
00:29:43,160 --> 00:29:46,240
You worked together
to help their team win.

316
00:29:47,040 --> 00:29:49,240
If you make me lose again,

317
00:29:49,320 --> 00:29:51,120
you'd better be ready.

318
00:29:53,400 --> 00:29:54,680
What are you going to do to him?

319
00:29:55,280 --> 00:29:56,640
What are you going to do to him?

320
00:29:57,440 --> 00:29:59,560
You two, watch your backs.

321
00:29:59,640 --> 00:30:01,600
- Want some, motherfucker?
- Tangmo! Stop!

322
00:30:01,680 --> 00:30:03,040
Tangmo! Stop!

323
00:30:04,400 --> 00:30:05,720
Hey, calm down.

324
00:30:09,720 --> 00:30:11,120
Tangmo.

325
00:30:11,200 --> 00:30:13,320
Look at me. Calm down.

326
00:30:23,000 --> 00:30:24,120
Forget it.

327
00:30:32,480 --> 00:30:35,640
<i>Pee's new romance novel</i>
<i>explores understanding</i>

328
00:30:35,720 --> 00:30:37,960
<i>and healing through simple</i>

329
00:30:38,040 --> 00:30:40,440
<i>yet profound conversations between</i>
<i>two people with different worldviews.</i>

330
00:30:40,520 --> 00:30:41,960
<i>One is sunshine,</i>

331
00:30:42,040 --> 00:30:43,480
<i>while the other is</i>
<i>the dark side of the moon.</i>

332
00:30:45,040 --> 00:30:46,640
You're such a boomer.

333
00:30:46,720 --> 00:30:48,400
Having AI read it aloud?

334
00:30:49,040 --> 00:30:51,240
Especially with this plot,

335
00:30:51,320 --> 00:30:52,440
it sounds so…

336
00:30:52,520 --> 00:30:53,720
What's the word?

337
00:30:53,800 --> 00:30:54,920
Surreal.

338
00:30:56,800 --> 00:30:58,440
The world keeps turning.

339
00:30:58,520 --> 00:31:00,240
We just adapt.

340
00:31:00,320 --> 00:31:01,640
I'm a slow reader.

341
00:31:01,720 --> 00:31:03,520
If there's a tool available, I'll use it.

342
00:31:04,640 --> 00:31:05,680
Soon enough,

343
00:31:05,760 --> 00:31:08,040
AI will probably take my job.

344
00:31:09,840 --> 00:31:12,240
Maybe I should retire now.

345
00:31:12,320 --> 00:31:14,120
Then I won't have to
rack my brain for ideas.

346
00:31:15,440 --> 00:31:18,760
Art, in the end, has to come from humans.

347
00:31:18,840 --> 00:31:20,640
AI is just a tool.

348
00:31:21,440 --> 00:31:23,200
Actually, I think you write well.

349
00:31:24,160 --> 00:31:25,440
Why are you so insecure?

350
00:31:26,120 --> 00:31:27,080
What?

351
00:31:27,160 --> 00:31:29,240
Didn't you say you were a slow reader?

352
00:31:29,320 --> 00:31:31,320
Are you just flattering me?

353
00:31:32,800 --> 00:31:35,800
Reading slowly doesn't mean I can't read.

354
00:31:36,640 --> 00:31:38,280
I've been reading your work.

355
00:31:39,120 --> 00:31:40,680
Your writing is really sharp.

356
00:31:40,760 --> 00:31:44,080
Like when Thanwa tells Kim,

357
00:31:44,720 --> 00:31:46,920
"Some people taught me to hold on."

358
00:31:47,440 --> 00:31:49,840
"Others taught me to let go."

359
00:31:50,520 --> 00:31:52,240
"But you're the only one

360
00:31:52,320 --> 00:31:54,720
who taught me both at once."

361
00:31:55,800 --> 00:31:56,960
That's so damn touching.

362
00:31:57,040 --> 00:31:58,040
It's so damn profound.

363
00:31:59,640 --> 00:32:04,000
Well, maybe because back then,
Pee helped me write it.

364
00:32:06,200 --> 00:32:07,920
But you're the main writer.

365
00:32:08,640 --> 00:32:10,040
Have some confidence in yourself.

366
00:32:10,120 --> 00:32:12,320
You're more talented than you think.

367
00:32:19,320 --> 00:32:20,920
I've decided to accept your offer.

368
00:32:24,400 --> 00:32:26,560
Huh? What did you say?

369
00:32:27,800 --> 00:32:29,200
Are you deaf?

370
00:32:30,240 --> 00:32:33,320
If you want me to be the model
for a character in your novel,

371
00:32:33,920 --> 00:32:34,840
I'll take the job.

372
00:32:36,240 --> 00:32:38,400
Are you trying to trick me again?

373
00:32:38,920 --> 00:32:40,600
I'm not lying to you.

374
00:32:41,200 --> 00:32:43,200
So when you decide to say yes,

375
00:32:43,280 --> 00:32:44,880
it's really that simple?

376
00:32:45,640 --> 00:32:49,040
If you're looking for someone
to make your novel perfect,

377
00:32:49,120 --> 00:32:52,840
maybe that someone is me.
Let me assure you,

378
00:32:52,920 --> 00:32:54,840
I can definitely do better than Pee.

379
00:32:56,120 --> 00:32:58,040
Yes! This calls for a celebration!

380
00:32:58,120 --> 00:32:59,480
My treat.

381
00:32:59,560 --> 00:33:00,680
Hey, wait.

382
00:33:00,760 --> 00:33:02,480
I have to drive back to Bangkok.

383
00:33:02,560 --> 00:33:03,560
Who cares?

384
00:33:03,640 --> 00:33:05,160
If you get drunk, stay another night.

385
00:33:05,240 --> 00:33:07,480
Come on. It's on me. Let's go.

386
00:33:09,400 --> 00:33:10,600
Calm down.

387
00:33:10,680 --> 00:33:12,360
The booze isn't going anywhere.

388
00:33:17,720 --> 00:33:18,800
Easy.

389
00:33:19,840 --> 00:33:21,720
You played rougher than this in hockey.

390
00:33:23,120 --> 00:33:24,800
Here, hold it.

391
00:33:31,440 --> 00:33:33,240
What did Au just say to you?

392
00:33:34,640 --> 00:33:35,840
He was just making threats.

393
00:33:36,400 --> 00:33:37,520
That's just his style.

394
00:33:40,320 --> 00:33:42,520
I can't protect you all the time.

395
00:33:43,120 --> 00:33:45,240
You need to get stronger.

396
00:33:45,320 --> 00:33:46,960
Don't let anyone hurt you.

397
00:33:48,000 --> 00:33:49,360
Why?

398
00:33:49,440 --> 00:33:50,920
Are you going to run away?

399
00:33:52,600 --> 00:33:54,920
If we can't escape,
we have to win the game, right?

400
00:33:56,520 --> 00:33:58,440
And there can only be one winner.

401
00:34:00,720 --> 00:34:01,720
Okay.

402
00:34:03,400 --> 00:34:04,520
What about the clue?

403
00:34:05,800 --> 00:34:07,520
Why should I tell you?

404
00:34:07,600 --> 00:34:09,120
I'm the one who won.

405
00:34:09,760 --> 00:34:11,280
For patching you up.

406
00:34:14,000 --> 00:34:15,560
Don't you want to get out of here soon?

407
00:34:16,960 --> 00:34:18,719
Two heads are better than one.

408
00:34:21,120 --> 00:34:22,920
The damn clue says "scholarship student."

409
00:34:25,920 --> 00:34:27,320
But from what I've figured out,

410
00:34:28,440 --> 00:34:30,040
I think we can rule out the women.

411
00:34:31,440 --> 00:34:32,639
Scholarship student…

412
00:34:34,320 --> 00:34:36,800
Nack's that old.
He's been out of high school for ages.

413
00:34:38,920 --> 00:34:40,960
As for Au and Wut,

414
00:34:41,040 --> 00:34:42,440
I don't think it's them.

415
00:34:44,920 --> 00:34:46,840
Then I think it's Cha.

416
00:34:46,920 --> 00:34:49,560
He had an athletic scholarship in college.

417
00:34:51,000 --> 00:34:53,560
And when the butler asked
if we wanted money or a clue,

418
00:34:53,639 --> 00:34:56,120
he immediately said he wanted the money.

419
00:34:57,360 --> 00:34:59,800
I bet he doesn't want anyone
to know he's a wolf.

420
00:35:01,800 --> 00:35:02,920
That's possible.

421
00:35:05,440 --> 00:35:07,240
Then let's vote for Cha tonight.

422
00:35:08,800 --> 00:35:09,800
He's the most likely suspect.

423
00:35:13,040 --> 00:35:14,720
If you see him die right in front of you,

424
00:35:15,720 --> 00:35:17,000
won't you feel anything?

425
00:35:20,040 --> 00:35:21,520
He used to be your friend.

426
00:35:23,920 --> 00:35:24,920
Friend?

427
00:35:26,920 --> 00:35:30,200
I used to think we were
the best hockey duo.

428
00:35:30,720 --> 00:35:32,800
Whenever we competed, we never lost.

429
00:35:34,200 --> 00:35:36,720
But out of nowhere, he blamed my father

430
00:35:36,800 --> 00:35:38,400
for not making the national team.

431
00:35:39,400 --> 00:35:41,520
So he quit and joined the opposing team

432
00:35:42,120 --> 00:35:43,720
to compete against me.

433
00:35:45,920 --> 00:35:47,440
What would you do?

434
00:35:50,000 --> 00:35:51,440
He was probably angry back then.

435
00:36:00,320 --> 00:36:03,240
Everyone I trusted fucking lied
to me and betrayed me.

436
00:36:05,720 --> 00:36:07,120
Whether it was Cha,

437
00:36:09,200 --> 00:36:10,240
my father,

438
00:36:12,160 --> 00:36:13,400
or even you.

439
00:36:36,400 --> 00:36:38,440
Cha! That's dangerous!

440
00:36:41,520 --> 00:36:42,840
You made the national team.

441
00:36:44,720 --> 00:36:46,520
Where did you hear that?

442
00:36:46,600 --> 00:36:47,920
They haven't announced it yet.

443
00:36:48,000 --> 00:36:50,840
Don't worry about how I found out.

444
00:36:50,920 --> 00:36:52,200
Just answer me.

445
00:36:52,280 --> 00:36:54,120
How much did your father pay

446
00:36:55,000 --> 00:36:56,720
to get your name on the list?

447
00:36:56,800 --> 00:36:58,760
What the fuck are you talking about?

448
00:36:58,840 --> 00:37:00,720
How many times have we competed together?

449
00:37:00,800 --> 00:37:02,760
We always won championships together.

450
00:37:02,840 --> 00:37:05,000
Are you saying those titles were fake?

451
00:37:05,080 --> 00:37:07,040
You're so naive.

452
00:37:07,120 --> 00:37:08,720
What the fuck?

453
00:37:08,800 --> 00:37:10,440
You might think you're good,

454
00:37:10,960 --> 00:37:14,240
but don't you know that the many
tournaments you won so easily

455
00:37:15,240 --> 00:37:17,400
were because your father
lobbied your opponents?

456
00:37:18,240 --> 00:37:19,520
Your father probably couldn't stand

457
00:37:20,840 --> 00:37:23,760
seeing his only son lose.

458
00:37:23,840 --> 00:37:25,240
Fine.

459
00:37:27,120 --> 00:37:29,880
I'll show you I can do it on my own.

460
00:37:29,960 --> 00:37:32,120
I'll withdraw from
the national team this time.

461
00:37:32,800 --> 00:37:35,360
Then you and I can win
this tournament together.

462
00:37:35,440 --> 00:37:38,240
I believe we'll both
make the national team.

463
00:37:38,920 --> 00:37:40,440
That day will never come.

464
00:37:41,240 --> 00:37:42,480
I'm transferring to another team.

465
00:37:44,040 --> 00:37:45,920
I don't want to live
in your shadow anymore.

466
00:37:50,240 --> 00:37:51,440
Oh.

467
00:37:52,720 --> 00:37:54,320
And here's a friendly warning.

468
00:37:56,440 --> 00:37:57,920
It's not just the hockey team

469
00:37:58,520 --> 00:37:59,920
your father's been interfering with.

470
00:38:06,000 --> 00:38:07,640
My father hired you, didn't he?

471
00:38:09,720 --> 00:38:11,200
My father hired you

472
00:38:11,280 --> 00:38:13,320
to be my boyfriend, didn't he?

473
00:38:14,800 --> 00:38:15,880
Answer me!

474
00:38:16,800 --> 00:38:18,400
At first, yes.

475
00:38:19,800 --> 00:38:22,800
But my feelings for you…
I really do love you.

476
00:38:26,440 --> 00:38:28,400
You say you love me…

477
00:38:31,000 --> 00:38:32,840
but you took a job from my father.

478
00:38:36,240 --> 00:38:38,520
Can you tell me the truth

479
00:38:39,840 --> 00:38:41,200
for once?

480
00:39:14,920 --> 00:39:16,280
I'm sorry.

481
00:39:33,240 --> 00:39:34,840
<i>When did you hire him, huh?</i>

482
00:39:36,200 --> 00:39:37,520
Just as you found out.

483
00:39:40,800 --> 00:39:42,400
How much did he pay you?

484
00:39:44,760 --> 00:39:46,800
How much did he pay you?

485
00:39:52,120 --> 00:39:53,160
Why did you do it?

486
00:39:53,840 --> 00:39:55,240
Why did you deceive me?

487
00:39:55,320 --> 00:39:58,120
Because I wanted you to take over TriCorp.

488
00:40:01,320 --> 00:40:02,320
TriCorp?

489
00:40:03,200 --> 00:40:05,280
Is TriCorp more important than my life?

490
00:40:05,360 --> 00:40:07,280
Do you still see me as your son?

491
00:40:07,360 --> 00:40:09,360
You all conspired to deceive me.

492
00:40:09,440 --> 00:40:10,880
Was it fun?

493
00:40:10,960 --> 00:40:12,600
You enjoyed it, didn't you?

494
00:40:13,840 --> 00:40:16,760
Isn't TriCorp the reason
you have everything you need?

495
00:40:25,440 --> 00:40:27,720
From now on, don't call me your son.

496
00:40:28,720 --> 00:40:30,360
And stay out of my life.

497
00:40:32,000 --> 00:40:33,200
Let me go.

498
00:40:40,040 --> 00:40:41,480
Tangmo…

499
00:41:01,720 --> 00:41:04,160
Everyone expresses love differently.

500
00:41:14,240 --> 00:41:16,200
Don't you want to reconcile with Cha?

501
00:41:17,720 --> 00:41:20,200
I can't change what's already happened.

502
00:41:21,440 --> 00:41:23,040
What about you and me?

503
00:41:33,640 --> 00:41:35,000
Just focus on surviving.

504
00:41:35,720 --> 00:41:37,120
We'll talk about the rest later.

505
00:41:53,520 --> 00:41:55,120
<i>Did you need something from me?</i>

506
00:41:56,200 --> 00:41:58,160
Tangmo is at the Crow Club.

507
00:41:59,000 --> 00:42:01,160
I want you to bring Tangmo home.

508
00:42:06,600 --> 00:42:07,680
I'm sorry.

509
00:42:08,600 --> 00:42:09,880
I can't do that for you.

510
00:42:10,840 --> 00:42:13,480
You'll have to handle this yourself.

511
00:42:22,920 --> 00:42:23,800
<i>Scholarship student.</i>

512
00:42:24,720 --> 00:42:27,920
- Who's a scholarship student?
- Well, it's not me.

513
00:42:28,560 --> 00:42:30,240
I heard

514
00:42:30,320 --> 00:42:32,840
- the wolf's a scholarship student?
- The clue's useless.

515
00:42:35,840 --> 00:42:37,400
I suspect Yoyeh.

516
00:42:37,480 --> 00:42:39,040
He seems smart.

517
00:42:39,920 --> 00:42:43,480
He probably worked with Tangmo
to make a plan.

518
00:42:43,560 --> 00:42:45,520
He made our team lose today.

519
00:42:46,720 --> 00:42:48,400
Cha was a scholarship student too.

520
00:42:48,480 --> 00:42:50,120
Aren't you suspicious of him?

521
00:42:50,720 --> 00:42:51,840
Are you messing with me?

522
00:42:52,520 --> 00:42:54,200
Then he's a scholarship student too.

523
00:42:54,280 --> 00:42:55,800
What does Yoyeh have to do with this?

524
00:42:55,880 --> 00:42:57,920
Didn't he get a scholarship
from your father?

525
00:42:59,120 --> 00:43:00,120
He got his money.

526
00:43:00,800 --> 00:43:02,480
That counts as a scholarship too.

527
00:43:02,560 --> 00:43:05,120
And you got a national team
athletic scholarship.

528
00:43:05,880 --> 00:43:08,920
If that's the case,
we can't rule anyone out.

529
00:43:13,800 --> 00:43:16,400
Welcome to the second night's wolf vote.

530
00:43:17,560 --> 00:43:18,760
Here he comes again.

531
00:43:25,720 --> 00:43:27,040
And now,

532
00:43:27,800 --> 00:43:29,640
the results of the second night's vote.

533
00:43:33,520 --> 00:43:34,360
Cha.

534
00:43:37,760 --> 00:43:38,920
Wut.

535
00:43:41,640 --> 00:43:42,720
Wut.

536
00:43:49,040 --> 00:43:49,920
Yoyeh.

537
00:43:55,880 --> 00:43:56,840
Yoyeh.

538
00:43:58,320 --> 00:43:59,160
Cha.

539
00:44:00,720 --> 00:44:01,560
Wut.

540
00:44:03,880 --> 00:44:04,800
And…

541
00:44:07,040 --> 00:44:08,240
Yoyeh.

542
00:44:13,400 --> 00:44:15,520
That means tonight,

543
00:44:17,120 --> 00:44:19,160
two people are tied in the vote.

544
00:45:02,920 --> 00:45:05,640
I'm begging you. Please don't shoot me.

545
00:45:05,720 --> 00:45:07,760
My mother is sick and bedridden.

546
00:45:07,840 --> 00:45:09,240
Please!

547
00:45:21,560 --> 00:45:24,120
Butler, didn't you say the rules…

548
00:46:12,480 --> 00:46:15,320
And the person the bodyguard
chose to protect tonight

549
00:46:17,120 --> 00:46:18,160
is Yoyeh.

550
00:46:22,120 --> 00:46:23,400
It's okay.

551
00:46:23,480 --> 00:46:25,520
It's okay now. You're safe.

552
00:46:27,520 --> 00:46:28,920
Get a hold of yourself.

553
00:46:29,800 --> 00:46:31,240
Stay calm.

554
00:46:31,840 --> 00:46:33,520
From this moment on,

555
00:46:34,880 --> 00:46:36,480
it's time for the wolves

556
00:46:37,200 --> 00:46:38,320
to hunt.

557
00:46:41,120 --> 00:46:42,480
Good luck, everyone.

558
00:46:44,880 --> 00:46:46,600
- He survived.
- Hope we all meet again tomorrow morning.

559
00:46:46,680 --> 00:46:47,920
Let's go.

560
00:47:08,720 --> 00:47:11,840
Yoyeh. Get a hold of yourself.

561
00:47:17,000 --> 00:47:19,120
I almost got killed instead of Wut.

562
00:47:19,720 --> 00:47:21,560
But you're still here.

563
00:47:21,640 --> 00:47:24,360
You're not dead. You're alive.

564
00:47:24,960 --> 00:47:26,040
Stay calm.

565
00:47:41,360 --> 00:47:42,760
Why are you here?

566
00:47:46,400 --> 00:47:49,720
I know you're the bodyguard.

567
00:47:51,400 --> 00:47:55,120
The only one who would write
Yoyeh's name to protect him is you.

568
00:47:56,520 --> 00:47:58,440
Same goes for Capture the Flag.

569
00:47:59,840 --> 00:48:01,320
Actually, I knew from day one.

570
00:48:03,720 --> 00:48:05,800
What I do is my business.

571
00:48:06,400 --> 00:48:07,720
Stay out of it.

572
00:48:09,320 --> 00:48:12,240
You really are as stubborn as ever.

573
00:48:13,120 --> 00:48:15,240
Have you ever actually played this game?

574
00:48:15,800 --> 00:48:18,240
The first person the wolves choose to hunt

575
00:48:19,600 --> 00:48:21,080
is the bodyguard.

576
00:48:21,160 --> 00:48:23,600
Because once the bodyguard dies,

577
00:48:27,520 --> 00:48:29,240
the villagers will have
no one to protect them.

578
00:48:35,400 --> 00:48:36,880
You'd better watch your backs.

579
00:48:43,440 --> 00:48:44,440
Let's go.

580
00:49:00,120 --> 00:49:02,240
Surprised? Razor-sharp.

581
00:49:08,000 --> 00:49:09,320
You're late.

582
00:49:10,040 --> 00:49:11,320
I went to get more weapons.

583
00:49:13,720 --> 00:49:16,160
Since you're both here,

584
00:49:16,760 --> 00:49:17,920
are either of you

585
00:49:18,920 --> 00:49:20,320
a wolf?

586
00:49:24,360 --> 00:49:26,560
- No.
- No.

587
00:49:30,120 --> 00:49:31,640
If I find out if anyone's lying,

588
00:49:32,200 --> 00:49:33,920
I'll hunt them down and kill them.

589
00:49:43,960 --> 00:49:45,640
You're not scared, are you?

590
00:49:51,000 --> 00:49:53,520
There can only be one winner anyway.

591
00:49:53,600 --> 00:49:55,520
Wolves or villagers,

592
00:49:55,600 --> 00:49:57,440
let's kill them all.

593
00:50:00,400 --> 00:50:02,840
How was that? I laughed like a villain.

594
00:50:04,720 --> 00:50:06,600
Come on, let's go hunting.

595
00:50:21,360 --> 00:50:22,720
- Don't follow me!
- Why are you running?

596
00:50:22,800 --> 00:50:25,360
- Aren't you tired? Just surrender!
- Don't follow me!

597
00:50:25,440 --> 00:50:26,640
Leave me alone!

598
00:50:26,720 --> 00:50:27,720
Go away!

599
00:50:30,120 --> 00:50:32,320
Don't! Help!

600
00:50:58,320 --> 00:50:59,520
We need to find somewhere to hide.

601
00:51:34,520 --> 00:51:36,040
Please don't hurt me.

602
00:51:38,400 --> 00:51:40,200
Let me go.

603
00:52:59,760 --> 00:53:01,480
<i>Everything is stated in the contract.</i>

604
00:53:01,560 --> 00:53:05,000
<i>Players must follow only</i>
<i>the rules of the game.</i>

605
00:53:05,080 --> 00:53:06,680
Then what about the people you've killed?

606
00:53:06,760 --> 00:53:09,240
- How the fuck is that allowed?
<i>- You do realize, don't you?</i>

607
00:53:09,320 --> 00:53:11,560
<i>Another death could happen here</i>
<i>at any moment.</i>

608
00:53:11,640 --> 00:53:13,400
<i>I still want to watch an exciting game</i>

609
00:53:13,480 --> 00:53:15,360
<i>played by the rules.</i>

610
00:53:15,440 --> 00:53:17,160
I'm sorry I brought you into this game.

611
00:53:17,240 --> 00:53:18,920
<i>I'll kill all the wolves,</i>

612
00:53:19,000 --> 00:53:21,080
and we'll both survive.

613
00:53:21,880 --> 00:53:23,160
<i>I think this reality show</i>

614
00:53:23,960 --> 00:53:25,160
is getting weird.

615
00:53:25,240 --> 00:53:27,000
<i>If I have to watch someone else kill you,</i>

616
00:53:27,080 --> 00:53:29,680
I'd rather be killed
by a monstrous ex like you.
